  "method": {
    "frame": "LAM lambda/beta/period/epoch/phase interpreted with the documented DAMIT and ADAM ecliptic-to-body rotation. UTC receive epoch from MJD-OBS, Horizons light-time-corrected geocentric vector, target spin at receive minus light time; Sun vector at target emission. Geocentre, not a fitted site-specific camera solution.",
    "pixels": "256 x 256 float64 primary FITS array; rows reversed into top-down display. Scale 3.63 mas per pixel from CD1_1. CRPIX 512 is outside the released cutout; initial centre 127.5,127.5 is diagnostic, followed by bounded limb fitting.",
    "display": "Linear 0-to-99.9th-percentile stretch; retains observed illumination and background. No absolute reflectance or natural-colour claim.",
    "projection": "Existing controlledShapeCamera, full source mesh ray intersections, interpolated vertex normals. Photograph transfer limited to lit, visible source geometry below 60 degrees emission; omitted samples shown grey. Virtual camera yaw changed 35 degrees, latitude multiplied by 0.65, range by 0.6. Offline nearest-pixel visualization only.",
    "limb": "Existing refineCameraByLimb with searchPixels 8, maximumControls 120, minimumControls 12, maximumCorrectionDegrees 0.01 and maximumResidualPixels 3. Disjoint edge holdouts; not interior controls.",
    "registration": "Existing registerCameraBands in checkOnly mode. Scratch comparison changes patch radius from 13 to 6 and sample step from 2 to 1; all correlation, fit-count and holdout limits unchanged. Radius 6 gives a 13-pixel patch, about 2.4 of the paper's nominal 20-mas resolution elements at the native 3.63-mas sampling. This is an exploratory parameter choice, not source-prescribed qualification.",
    "reproductionLimit": "The camera-derivation and rendering driver is an ignored exploratory script, not a supported preparation recipe. This record pins its source inputs, derived cameras, parameters and results; it is not a clean-checkout surface reproduction claim."
